  "title": "María, Ven --- Naming Who You Are Talking To",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:cac453291b9c3c79",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C64-maria-ven",
      "sequence": 2480,
      "title": "María, ven — naming who you are talking to",
      "headword": "María, ven",
      "romanization": "María, ven",
      "gloss": "María, come — naming the person you are speaking to, and the comma that is the whole of the grammar",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:de9887469704e879",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ven — come. ¿Cómo estás? — how are you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Both are aimed at somebody. Now say who."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the comma is the grammar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "María, ven. ¿Cómo estás, María? Profesor, ¿puedo hablar?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The name can go at the front or at the end, and either way it is fenced off by a comma. That comma is not decoration — it is the entire grammatical marking. There is nothing else to learn here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin had a whole case for this — a set of endings whose only job was addressing somebody. Spanish replaced all of it with a pause."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the shortest possible summary of what became of Latin's endings. Twice now you have watched the same thing: the endings went, and something small and audible took over the work — a preposition for the personal a, and here a comma."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And notice the person you address takes no a. Veo a María has María on the receiving end of the seeing; María, ven has her doing the coming. Same name, opposite roles, and the comma is what tells them apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "María, ven",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *María, ven*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Veo a María, then María, ven, and hear the difference",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Veo a María*, then *María, ven*, and hear the difference]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C64-maria-ven-say",
              "prompt": "Tell Maria to come, naming her first.",
              "assesses": [
